      "patched_sha256": "77870b1ca8c93223075a67076ffdee489821bda8aace060c93b1c7f6bf54e051",
      "reason": "The scalar scan was ~40k math.floor calls per lift and the largest GIL-holding block in the relocalizer, which starves the CPU fast loop running in the same process. Measured on RTX 5060 over 26 real P157 frames: localize_array p50 254.1 -> 174.1 ms (-31.5%), with status, inliers, inlier_ratio, reprojection_p90, anchor Point3D IDs and the cam_from_world bytes identical on every frame. Equivalence is pinned by tests/localization/deploy/test_lift_reference_matches.py, which keeps the pre-vectorisation body as a differential oracle. Admitted by README.md 'vendor 來源與搬遷規則' rule 3 as a measured optimisation; still owed upstream before the next re-vendor.",
